Package: python3-periph
Section: python
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: python3-smbus2, python3-spidev, python3-libgpiod (>= 2), python3-serial, python3-periphery
Description: peripheral chip drivers for Linux hosts (Python 3)
 Periph drives sensors, displays, converters, motor drivers and other
 peripheral chips over I2C, SPI, UART and GPIO. Each chip has a Minimal
 class that works out of the box and a Full class with the complete chip
 functionality; all values are in SI units.
 .
 This package contains the Python 3 module. The recommended packages provide
 the Linux bus access (/dev/i2c-N, spidev, libgpiod v2, serial ports).

Package: libperiph-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libgpiod-dev (>= 2), ${misc:Depends}
Description: peripheral chip drivers for Linux hosts (C++ development files)
 Periph drives sensors, displays, converters, motor drivers and other
 peripheral chips over I2C, SPI, UART and GPIO. Each chip has a Minimal
 class that works out of the box and a Full class with the complete chip
 functionality; all values are in SI units.
 .
 This package contains the static library libperiph.a, the C++17 headers,
 a pkg-config file (periph) and a CMake package (find_package(periph),
 target periph::periph).

Package: sigrok-decoders-periph
Section: electronics
Architecture: all
Depends: libsigrokdecode4, ${misc:Depends}
Enhances: sigrok-cli, pulseview
Description: sigrok protocol decoders for the Periph chips
 Protocol decoders for libsigrokdecode that stack on the i2c, spi and uart
 decoders and annotate register-level traffic of the peripheral chips
 supported by Periph (sensors, displays, converters, motor drivers and more).
 They show up in sigrok-cli and PulseView like the built-in decoders.
